- User Defined Classes & Operations (Introduction) -
-----------------------------------------------------

We have seen how to define classes of objects that know things - objects with state (i.e. attributes stored in 
variables). Next we will introduce classes of objects that can also do things.

Perhaps our bunnies should be able to hop, and eat, and sleep. Let's add a couple of operations (things that a bunny 
can do) to our Bunny class, and update our class diagram with a third compartment for the operations.

	------------------------
	|	Bunny	       |
	|	 age	       |
	|	 name          |
	------------------------
	|	hop()          |
	|	eat()	       |
	|	sleep()	       |
	------------------------

We add operations to a class in java by defining methods inside the class. Let's add a hop method, and an eat method, and a sleep method to our Bunny class. Let's also say that we must pass some food (as a String argument) when we 
call the eat method.

